      "gitCommit": {
        "shortHash": "32440ba",
        "hash": "32440ba8d3b364318a9f223e010648832380632d",
        "subject": "Drop the false duplicate note, explain the PDF password",
        "body": "Drop the false duplicate note, explain the PDF password\n\nThe upload sheet claimed \"Solo se importan transacciones nuevas. Los duplicados\nse omiten automáticamente.\" That is not what happens. When the importer finds\nduplicates, `Statements::StatusManager#determine_status` returns `:parsed` with\nthe comment \"user needs to review in pending_transactions\" — they are queued for\nthe user to decide on, not silently skipped. The note told people an action was\nhandled for them when it was not, so it is removed. The success screen already\nreports \"{{new}} nuevas · {{dupes}} pendientes de revisión\", which is accurate.\n\n(The swipe deck is `transfer_candidates` — pairing transfers between accounts —\nwhich is a different mechanism from duplicate detection.)\n\nThe PDF password field now carries a note that the password is only used to open\nthe file and is not kept. That claim is safe to make: `clear_password!` runs in\nthe `ensure` block of `Statements::Processor`, so it fires on failure paths too,\nand the column is `encrypts`-ed at rest in the meantime. The note renders only\nwhen the field is disclosed, so the sheet stays short for the common case.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n",
        "author": {
          "name": "Nived Vengilat",
          "email": "nivedvengilat@gmail.com",
          "time": 1787101884000
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Nived Vengilat",
          "email": "nivedvengilat@gmail.com",
          "time": 1787101884000
        },
        "branch": "HEAD"
      },
